  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: IGC Urban Economics Data Conference</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SGCI Convening Fund promotes development in ODA eligible countries. The Urban Economics Data Conference will bring together academics, policy makers, and development practitioners to discuss how economics research can help inform urban policy decisions and the allocation of scarce resources to build productive, liveable, and sustainable cities in Africa. The objectives of this conference tie neatly with the UK priorities in Southern Africa for inclusive economic growth as well as the existing ODA programmes supporting local economic development in cities. In South Africa, this requires increased knowledge and capacity to integrate scientific evidence on urban economics which is currently lacking across the region. Due to limited awareness and access to resources within African practitioners in the field of economics data and urban policy, it is critical that this conference and Winter School is able to secure participation from much needed African perspectives on the subject and increase engagement with the Global South. The funding will allow selected African practitioners, policy makers and researchers to participate in this conference.
Collectively, UK&#x2019;s funding of selected researchers and policymakers at the event can strengthen the role of Africa in driving these debates with contextual knowledge and understanding of the challenges faced by African cities.</narrative>
  </description>
